  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "MSRVs BFN-3-PCV-001-0004, BFN-3-PCV-001-0022, BFN-3-PCV-001-0034, and BFN-3-PCV-001-0041 failed due to corrosion bonding to the valve seats and non-quantifiable leakage known as simmering. As a result of corrosion bonding, the force required to break the crystal structure of the corrosion bond alters the mechanical setpoint of the pilot valve...Simmering valves results in mechanical setpoint drift and is generally the result of low stellite in the seat.",
